00:09:37,142 --> 00:09:43,142
Zathura: A Space Adventure is a science fiction,
adventure, family film directed by Jon Favreau.

3
00:14:25,714 --> 00:14:31,714
After their father is called into work, two young boys, Walter and Danny, are left in
the care of their teenage sister, Lisa, and told they must stay inside.

4
00:19:14,285 --> 00:19:20,285
Walter and Danny, who anticipate a boring day, are shocked when they begin playing Zathura, a space-themed
board game, which they realize has mystical powers when their house is shot into space.

5
00:24:02,857 --> 00:24:08,857
With the help of an astronaut, the boys attempt to return home.

6
00:28:51,428 --> 00:28:57,428
Walter Budwing, played by Josh Hutcherson.

7
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:46,000
Danny Budwing, played by Jonah Bobo.

8
00:38:28,571 --> 00:38:34,571
Astronaut, played by Dax Shepard.

9
00:43:17,142 --> 00:43:23,142
Lisa Budwing, played by Kristen Stewart.

10
00:48:05,714 --> 00:48:11,714
Dad (Mr. Budwing), played by Tim Robbins.

11
00:52:54,285 --> 00:53:00,285
Robot (voice), played by Frank Oz.

12
00:57:42,857 --> 00:57:48,857
Zathura: A Space Adventure (or simply Zathura) is a 2005 American science fiction
action-adventure film directed by Jon Favreau and written by David Koepp and John Kamps.

13
01:02:31,428 --> 01:02:37,428
It is an adaptation of the 2002 children's book Zathura by Chris Van
Allsburg, author of the 1981 children's book Jumanji.

14
01:07:20,000 --> 01:07:26,000
It is a standalone spin-off of the 1995 film Jumanji and the
second installment of the Jumanji franchise.

15
01:12:08,571 --> 01:12:14,571
The film stars Josh Hutcherson and Jonah Bobo as two squabbling brothers who find a mysterious board game in the basement
which transports their house into outer space, and must survive and finish the game in order to return home.

16
01:16:57,142 --> 01:17:03,142
Dax Shepard, Kristen Stewart, and Tim Robbins are also among the cast.

17
01:21:45,714 --> 01:21:51,714
Zathura was shot in Los Angeles and Culver City, California, and was released on
November 11, 2005, in the United States by Sony Pictures Releasing.

18
01:26:34,285 --> 01:26:40,285
It received positive reviews from critics and grossed $65.1
million worldwide against a $65 million budget.

19
01:31:22,857 --> 01:31:28,857
The film explores themes of fire, based on novel or
book, killer robot, house, space travel.

20
01:36:11,428 --> 01:36:17,428
The tone is thought_provoking.
